 ## Overview
-This method performs 3D pathfinding on a Sparse Voxel Octree (SVO) by combining A* search with Lazy Theta* logic, where line-of-sight (LOS) checks are performed optimistically during neighbor expansion to allow straight-line shortcuts, with a recovery step if LOS fails. It differs from standard A* on octrees by reducing path length and node visits through direct parent-to-current-node connections when possible, and differs from pure ray-casting pathfinding by caching collision results to avoid expensive per-step ray-marching.
+This method performs 3D pathfinding on a Sparse Voxel Octree (SVO) by combining A* search with Lazy Theta* logic, where line-of-sight (LOS) checks are performed optimistically during neighbor expansion to allow straight-line shortcuts, with a recovery step if LOS fails [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard A* on octrees by reducing path length and node visits through direct parent-to-current-node connections when possible, and differs from pure ray-casting pathfinding by caching collision results to avoid expensive per-step ray-marching [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Octree Path Computation](897-octree-path-computation.md) and operates alongside [Octree Neighbor Search](7782-octree-neighbor-search.md) and [Access Path Predictor](11650-access-path-predictor.md).
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-- **Input:** Start and End world positions, Agent Radius, SVO structure (node array, depth, traversal data).
-- **Output:** Sequence of nodes forming the path, or failure if no path exists.
